GeneralsX @bugfix Android port 13/09/2026

Let GetLocalAddresses() use getifaddrs() on Android.

Android is excluded from the POSIX branch, so the function falls through to
AssertMsg(false, "Write me!") and returns false. Its only caller is the ICE
session's interface gathering:

    void CSteamNetworkingICESession::GatherInterfaces()
    {
        CUtlVector<LocalAddress_t> vecAddrs;
        if ( !GetLocalAddresses( &vecAddrs ) )
            return;

Everything ICE does is per-interface -- host candidates, STUN binding
requests, TURN allocations, and the sending of packets itself. With no
interfaces there are no candidates of any kind, no STUN traffic and no TURN
traffic, and a peer connection can only ever time out. A device log of a
failed match shows that exact assert firing 293 times, once per gathering
attempt, for the whole duration of the connect.

The exclusion looks like "nobody wrote it" rather than a real limitation:
bionic has had getifaddrs()/freeifaddrs() since API 24 (Android 7.0), this
port's minSdk is 28, and the engine beside it already enumerates interfaces
this way (Core/GameEngine/Source/GameNetwork/IPEnumeration.cpp).

This is not a problem upstream's Windows client can hit -- it builds
GameNetworkingSockets with USE_STEAMWEBRTC=ON and never compiles this ICE
client at all. This port is the first user of Valve's native one.

bionic ships <ifaddrs.h> too, and the header was hidden behind the same
assumption, so the include guard has to go with it or the source above will
not compile.

--- a/src/steamnetworkingsockets/clientlib/steamnetworkingsockets_socketthread.cpp
+++ b/src/steamnetworkingsockets/clientlib/steamnetworkingsockets_socketthread.cpp
@@ -4221,7 +4221,7 @@
     free( pAddrInfo );
 	return true;
 
-#elif IsPosix() && !IsPlaystation() && !IsAndroid() && !IsNintendoSwitch()
+#elif IsPosix() && !IsPlaystation() && !IsNintendoSwitch()
 
 	ifaddrs *pMyAddrInfo = NULL;
 	int r = getifaddrs( &pMyAddrInfo );

--- a/src/public/tier0/platform_sockets.h
+++ b/src/public/tier0/platform_sockets.h
@@ -87,9 +87,7 @@
 	#include <poll.h>
 	#include <errno.h>
 
-	#if !IsAndroid()
 		#include <ifaddrs.h>
-	#endif
 	#include <net/if.h>
 
 	#ifndef closesocket
